  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1045 PM CDT Tue Jul 21 2026\n\nBy Friday, we start to see some additional energy interact with this \nboundary near the AL/TN state line. This will bring rain chances \nback to the area and keep temperatures below average through the \nfirst part of the upcoming weekend. The best/most widespread rain \nchances will be Friday night into Saturday. At this time, I don't \nsee any severe weather indicators.\n\nOnce the rain tapers off Saturday evening, long term guidance is \nsuggesting the influences of ridging over the center of the country \nshould shut off our rain chances and start to increase\ntemperatures. There are some model differences in this happening,\nso fine tuning will be needed over the next several days \nregarding the forecast for the second half of the weekend into the\nstart of next week.",
